From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: per-app data accounting on the 4.19 kernel

netd attaches the per-app traffic accounting, the per-app firewall and the
socket hooks to the cgroup root in BpfHandler::initPrograms. Android 16 (25Q2)
returns from it before attaching anything when the kernel is older than 5.4,
so on this phone no app ever had data usage and the per-app restrictions were
never enforced; the 4.19 variants of those programs are still built and the
loader still loads them. Attach them on a 4.19 kernel instead of giving up.
---
diff --git a/bpf/netd/BpfHandler.cpp b/bpf/netd/BpfHandler.cpp
--- a/bpf/netd/BpfHandler.cpp
+++ b/bpf/netd/BpfHandler.cpp
@@ -92,8 +92,12 @@
     }
 
     // 25Q2 bumps the kernel requirement up to 5.4
+    // Kompakt: the 4.19 programs are still built and loaded; on this 4.19 kernel attach them.
     if (isAtLeast25Q2 && !isAtLeastKernelVersion(5, 4)) {
-        return Status("25Q2+ platform with kernel version < 5.4.0 is unsupported");
+        if (!isAtLeastKernelVersion(4, 19)) {
+            return Status("25Q2+ platform with kernel version < 4.19.0 is unsupported");
+        }
+        ALOGW("Kompakt: 25Q2+ platform on a 4.19 kernel, attaching the 4.19 programs");
     }
 
     unique_fd cg_fd(open(cg2_path, O_DIRECTORY | O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC));
